================================================================================
Data / rule lists
================================================================================

- backend/src/services/germanAbbreviations.ts contains German + English
  abbreviation, unit, and symbol expansion rules inspired by
  repodiac/german_transliterate (CC-BY 4.0,
  https://github.com/repodiac/german_transliterate). Rules were
  reimplemented in TypeScript and extended with PageMentor-specific
  entries (Studienheft conventions, §§, Abb./Tab. formatting).

  Per CC-BY 4.0: copyright 2020 repodiac, licensed under Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 International. See
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ for terms.
- Kokoro-FastAPI-German (Apache 2.0) https://github.com/r1di/kokoro-fastapi-german
  optional second TTS sidecar exposing the German community voices
  df_eva + dm_bernd. Built on Tundragoon/Kokoro-German v1.1
  (Apache 2.0, https://huggingface.co/Tundragoon/Kokoro-German),
  fine-tuned on the HUI-Audio-Corpus-German dataset, with espeak-ng
  as the phonemizer backend.

================================================================================
Third-party service: Microsoft Edge Read-Aloud API (Azure Neural TTS)
================================================================================

PageMentor uses Microsoft's Edge Read-Aloud endpoint via the msedge-tts
client library. The API is publicly reachable but is not officially
documented for third-party use. The Microsoft Neural voice models
themselves are proprietary and remain the property of Microsoft / Azure.

- Voice playback is rate-limited and intended for personal, non-commercial
  use of the kind a browser user would generate with Microsoft Edge.
- Large-scale automated use may violate Microsoft's terms of service.

If you need guaranteed-compliant TTS, use the bundled Kokoro sidecar
instead (Apache 2.0, runs locally — see docker-compose.yml). Edge stays
available as a no-setup fallback.

